+   SPECIFICITY: `:global(:root[data-frame="color"]) .tile` is (0,4,0) against the
+   base `.tile` (0,1,0), so it wins on specificity alone rather than on module
+   order. `.tileUnit` is TRIPLED in the base rule to clear `.btn.ghost`, so the
+   Pastel override triples it too — an untripled override would be (0,4,0)
+   against the base's (0,4,0) and would depend on source order.
+   ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */
+
+:global(:root[data-frame="color"]) .tile {
+  /* 22% toward white — the handoff's own subject-tint ratio. */
+  background: linear-gradient(
